@startuml Kiwi_Observation_Scoring
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Latin Modern Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #216875
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 24
title Proposed scoring decisions for each scheduled receiver / burst observation
top to bottom direction
rectangle "Scheduled observation\n+ expected-frame identity" as Planned
rectangle "Full transmission\nconfirmed?" as TX
rectangle "TX unconfirmed / partial\nnot an expected full frame" as NoTX
 rectangle "Capture available\nand decode-eligible?" as Valid
rectangle "Infrastructure / capture outcome\nretain reason; exclude from RF denominator" as Invalid
 rectangle "Exact expected\nframe recovered?" as Exact
rectangle "Exact recovery\ncount expected identity once" as Pass
rectangle "Valid RF/decode miss\ninclude in RF denominator" as Miss
Planned -right-> TX
TX --> NoTX : no
TX -right-> Valid : yes
Valid --> Invalid : no
Valid -right-> Exact : yes
Exact --> Pass : yes
Exact --> Miss : no
note bottom of Miss
A valid recording with no acquired
burst is still a miss.
Record duplicates and conflicting CRC-
valid frames separately.
Decode success must not decide capture
eligibility.
end note
@enduml
